    "body": "fix on issue/4241-kernel-link-edge-band · PR #4253 · pinned by link_rule::a_link_in_the_edge_band_over_uncut_stock_is_refused, link_rule::a_link_in_the_edge_band_near_a_keep_out_is_refused, link_rule::a_link_beside_a_part_that_reaches_out_of_the_stock_is_refused, link_rule::a_link_leaves_a_cut_at_the_stock_edge_runs_in_the_air_and_comes_back_over_cleared_stock · merges when reviewed\n\nThe lift counts do not change (disc band 13, dog-bone band 15, Outside). Each lift on the disc is at the start of a piece that no cut has touched: the way back in is not within the swath of a cut made. The decision `docs/decisions/4241-kernel-link-edge-band.md` names the missing proof of each lift. The fix also closes a gap: the air of an Outside region now leaves out the part grown by the tool radius, so a link in the air cannot cross a part that reaches out of the stock.",
